Customer Segmentation & Predictive Marketing App – Documentation

1. Project Overview
This project is a real-world Data Science pipeline for e-commerce businesses.
It allows users to upload customer data, perform segmentation, and predict campaign response with an interactive Streamlit web app.

Business Problem:
Businesses have thousands of customers, but their behavior differs. Some are loyal, some shop occasionally, and some only during discounts.
This project helps analyze customer behavior to make smarter marketing decisions.

2. Features

RFM feature calculation from transactions (Recency, Frequency, Monetary value)

Customer Segmentation using K-Means clustering

Predictive Marketing using Random Forest classifier

Interactive visualizations with Plotly

Simple UI with Streamlit (upload CSV, see results instantly)

Fully deployable online on Streamlit Cloud

3. Dataset Format

Column Name	Description
Customer No.	Unique customer identifier
Qty	Quantity purchased
Sold Price	Price per item
Purchase Date	Date of transaction
Job No.	Unique transaction number

Optional columns: Customer Name, Category, Email, etc.

4. Getting Started (Local Setup)

Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/customer-segmentation-app.git
cd customer-segmentation-app


Create a virtual environment:

python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate   # Mac/Linux
venv\Scripts\activate      # Windows


Install dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt


Run the Streamlit app:

streamlit run Marketing_App.py


Open browser at http://localhost:8501

5. Deployment on Streamlit Cloud

Push repository to GitHub

Go to Streamlit Cloud
 → New app → Select repo → Branch main → File: Marketing_App.py

Click Deploy → Public URL will be generated

Share link for live interaction

6. Folder Structure

customer-segmentation-app/
│
├── Marketing_App.py        # Streamlit app
├── requirements.txt        # Python dependencies
├── README.md               # Project description
├── sample_dataset.csv      # Optional sample CSV for testing


7. Technologies Used

Python 3.13

Pandas & NumPy

Scikit-learn (KMeans, RandomForest)

Plotly (interactive visualization)

Streamlit (UI & deployment)

